COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[22,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nInciting crisis and exaggerating issues are the works of hypocrites and disbelievers. Warn the community in a message containing three issues in which the media used these methods.\nIdentify a trial through which Muslims became confused and unable to distinguish truth from falsehood, and ask Allah to guide you to the truth.\nAdvise someone who is heedless of his prayers that Allah called the prayer: faith, and that He will hold everyone accountable for establishing prayers.\nguid\nA foolish person is one who objects to the rule of Allah.\nThe test of your good faith is to adhere to the commands of Allah, submitting to Him and accepting His judgment, whether or not you know the wisdom behind it.\nDifferentiate between winning the hearts of those whom you call to the right path, and following their desires by doing something that incurs the wrath of Allah.\nrefl\nسَيَقُولُ ٱلسُّفَهَآءُ مِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَا وَلَّىٰهُمۡ عَن قِبۡلَتِهِمُ ٱلَّتِي كَانُواْ عَلَيۡهَاۚ\nA wise person pays no attention to the objections of a fool and does not worry about him. This verse indicates that no one objects to the rulings of Allah but one who is foolish, ignorant and stubborn. As for the wise and rational believer, he accepts the rulings of his Lord and submits to them, as Allah says, (It is not fitting for any believing man or believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decided concerning a matter, to have any choice in that matter) [33:36]. (But no, by your Lord, they will not [truly] believe until they make you [O Muhammad] judge in all disputes between them, then find in their hearts no reservations about your verdicts, but accept them wholeheartedly) [4:65]. Al-Saadi: 70.\nWhat is the true believer's position on Islamic rulings?\nسَيَقُولُ ٱلسُّفَهَآءُ مِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَا وَلَّىٰهُمۡ عَن قِبۡلَتِهِمُ ٱلَّتِي كَانُواْ عَلَيۡهَاۚ\nInforming Muslims about something that is yet to occur in order to ease its impact on them when it happens, since being aware of an unpleasant thing ahead of time makes it less disruptive. Moreover, it enables Muslims to confute their adversaries. Al-Alusi: 2/2.\nAllah informed Muslims about what would be said before its occurrence. Why?\nسَيَقُولُ ٱلسُّفَهَآءُ مِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَا وَلَّىٰهُمۡ عَن قِبۡلَتِهِمُ ٱلَّتِي كَانُواْ عَلَيۡهَاۚ قُل لِّلَّهِ ٱلۡمَشۡرِقُ وَٱلۡمَغۡرِبُۚ\nThe fact that Allah describes them as (foolish) is sufficient to reject what they say, with no need for further refutation. But Allah did not leave this specious argument without dispelling it and highlighting the flaws in the argument that may influence some people. Hence, He said, (Say: To Allah belong the east and the west). Al-Saadi: 70.\nIs it sufficient to call those who object to Islamic rulings \"fools\" without refuting their weak arguments?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلۡنَٰكُمۡ أُمَّةٗ وَسَطٗا\nThe word (Wasat), used in this verse, means the best and the most excellent. When Allah made this Ummah (Muslim nation) a (Wasat), He has distinguished it with the perfect laws, the best methods and the clearest beliefs. Ibn Kathir: 1/181.\nHow does the verse indicate the superiority of Islam over other religions?\nوَلَئِنۡ أَتَيۡتَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ بِكُلِّ ءَايَةٖ مَّا تَبِعُواْ قِبۡلَتَكَۚ\nEven if the Prophet (r) were to bring to the People of the Scripture (Jews and Christians) all the proofs to the truth of his Message, they would not follow him nor abandon their desires, as Allah says, (Indeed, those upon whom the decree of Allah is passed will not believe. even if every sign were to come to them, until they see the painful torment) [10:96]. That is why He says here, (And if you brought to those who were given the Scripture every sign, they would not follow your Qiblah). Ibn Kathir: 1/184.\nGuidance is a favor from Allah and not just a convincing of the mind. Explain.\nوَلَئِنۡ أَتَيۡتَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ بِكُلِّ ءَايَةٖ مَّا تَبِعُواْ قِبۡلَتَكَۚ وَمَآ أَنتَ بِتَابِعٖ قِبۡلَتَهُمۡۚ وَمَا بَعۡضُهُم بِتَابِعٖ قِبۡلَةَ بَعۡضٖۚ\nThis shows that their opposition and obstinacy is not limited to you, but rather due to their nature of extreme obstinacy even among themselves. Al-Alusi: 2/12.\nAre the views and doubts of the disbelievers and hypocrites the result of logical thinking? Explain.\nوَلَئِنِ ٱتَّبَعۡتَ أَهۡوَآءَهُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَكَ مِنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ إِنَّكَ إِذٗا لَّمِنَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٤٥\nAllah warns against a scholar who knows the truth yet he follows his desires, since his knowledge of the truth will be used as an argument against him in the Hereafter. Ibn Kathir: 1/184.\nWhy is one's knowledge singled out for warning and threat?\nwords\nيَنقَلِبُ عَلَى عَقِبَيهِRenounces his faith"],[23,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nHasten today to be in the first row for a prayer, the first to give to charity or the first to recite the Quran, as forerunners have greater rewards.\nSay: \"O my Lord, increase me in knowledge, purity and wisdom.\"\nKeep reading your Athkar in the morning, evening, after prayers and teach them to others.\nguid\nWhoever is satisfied with the minimum limit of doing good deeds, his drive will weaken to the point of laziness; but whoever commits himself to be ahead of others, will be steadfast and closer to Allah.\nThe servant should not think that he can escape from Allah's power through the use of means, for Allah is the Most Capable over him at any place and time.\nThe best two remedies when facing calamities are patience and prayer.\nrefl\nفَٱسۡتَبِقُواْ ٱلۡخَيۡرَٰتِۚ\nThe one who takes this initiative in this world will be the first to attain Paradise in the Hereafter, and those who are foremost in the race will be the highest in status. This verse is used as evidence for doing all kinds of good deeds, such as offering prayer on time; hastening to do what is required of fasting, Hajj, Umrah and paying zakah; offering Sunnah acts of worship and so on. How comprehensive and beneficial this verse is!! Al-Saadi: 73.\nThis verse has few words with ample meanings. Explain.\nوَمِنۡ حَيۡثُ خَرَجۡتَ فَوَلِّ وَجۡهَكَ شَطۡرَ ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِۖ وَإِنَّهُۥ لَلۡحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكَۗ\nWhoever turns his heart in his prayer to other than his Lord, his body's direction toward the Ka'ba will not benefit him, because that is a true ruling, the reality of which is the direction of the heart. Therefore, whoever turns his heart toward any of the creation in his prayer is like someone whose face has been turned away from his Qiblah. Al-Biqai: 1/272.\nWhat is truth about turning toward the Qiblah in prayer? And why?\nفَٱذۡكُرُونِيٓ أَذۡكُرۡكُمۡ وَٱشۡكُرُواْ لِي وَلَا تَكۡفُرُونِ ١٥٢\nEvery remembrance of Allah has its own characteristic and fruit. Tahlīl is saying: (No deity is worthy of worship but Allah) results in acquiring Tawhīd. I mean specific monotheism, as general monotheism is attained by all believers. Takbīr is saying, (Allah Akbar) results in glorification and veneration of the Most High. As for the praise and names that mean benevolence and mercy, such as the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, the Most Generous, the Most Forgiving, and the like result in acquiring three levels of heart deeds: Gratitude, strength of hope, and love of Allah since every doer of good is surely loved. Ibn Juzay: 1/88.\nFor every remembrance, there is a fruitful result in the heart. Explain.\nفَٱذۡكُرُونِيٓ أَذۡكُرۡكُمۡ وَٱشۡكُرُواْ لِي وَلَا تَكۡفُرُونِ ١٥٢\nEvery remembrance of Allah has its own characteristic and fruit. As for holy Names signifying knowledge and awareness such as The All-Knowing, the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing, the Near, etc., their fruit is observance. Praying for Allah's blessings upon the Prophet (r) results in intense love for him and maintaining adherence to his Sunnah. Asking for Allah's forgiveness results in steadfastness in righteousness, and preservation of the conditions of repentance while maintaining humbleness due to past sins. Ibn Juzay: 1/88.\nWhat are the results of remembering Allah by His Names: The All-Hearing, the All-Seeing and the Near?\nوَٱشۡكُرُواْ لِي وَلَا تَكۡفُرُونِ ١٥٢ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱسۡتَعِينُواْ بِٱلصَّبۡرِ وَٱلصَّلَوٰةِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ١٥٣\nAfter Allah commands that He be offered gratitude, He ordains patience and prayer. The servant is either in a blessing for which he is grateful, or in a calamity for which he endures patiently. Ibn Kathir: 1/187.\nThe servant of Allah experiences two states. What are they? What is his duty during each state?\nٱسۡتَعِينُواْ بِٱلصَّبۡرِ وَٱلصَّلَوٰةِۚ\nIf a servant's prayer is complete, combining what is required and what is recommended, and it is done with the presence of heart, then there is no doubt that this prayer is one of the greatest aids in all his affairs. For prayer restrains one from immorality and wrongdoing, because this presence that occurs during prayer creates in the servant's heart a quality that leads him to comply with his Lord's commands and heed His prohibitions. This is the prayer through which Allah has enjoined us to seek help in all our affairs. Al-Saadi: 75.\nHow does the prayer help one comply with his Lord's commands and heed His prohibitions?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ١٥٣\n(Allah is with those), this is indicative of Allah's love, help, support and closeness, and it is a great privilege that is bestowed upon those who are patient. If those who are patient did not have any virtue other than the fact that Allah is with them, it would be sufficient honor and privilege for them. Al-Saadi: 75.\nWhat is the meaning of this statement (Allah is with those)? Who are worthy of it? Explain.\nwords\nالمُمتَرِينَThose who doubt"],[24,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nAsk Allah for martyrdom sincerely from your heart.\nWhen hearing about misfortunes of Muslims on the news, say: \"We belong to Allah, and to Him we will return.\"\nAsk Allah for safety, then memorize the recommended supplication when a calamity befalls: Whoever suffers a calamity and says: \"We belong to Allah, and to Him we will return\"; O Allah, reward me for my calamity and replace it with something better; Allah will replace it with something better for him.\nguid\nA believer who is afflicted with calamities in himself, his family or wealth, and he remains patient, his status and rank will be high with his Lord.\nConcealing knowledge and truth results in being cursed and expelled from the mercy of Allah, the Almighty.\nAn evil scholar is cursed by all those who curse, while a righteous scholar has all supplicants asking for Allah's forgiveness for him.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ١٥٣ وَلَا تَقُولُواْ لِمَن يُقۡتَلُ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ أَمۡوَٰتُۢ بَلۡ أَحۡيَآءٞ وَلَٰكِن لَّا تَشۡعُرُونَ ١٥٤\nThis is an indication that Allah is being with them does not keep some from becoming martyrs; in fact, that is one of the fruits of being with Allah, as those who are martyred will attain eternal happiness in the Hereafter, and those who remain will attain happiness in this world and the Hereafter. Al-Biqai: 1/279.\nIs the fact that Allah is being with patient fighters would keep them from becoming martyrs?\nوَلَا تَقُولُواْ لِمَن يُقۡتَلُ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ أَمۡوَٰتُۢ بَلۡ أَحۡيَآءٞ وَلَٰكِن لَّا تَشۡعُرُونَ ١٥٤\nIt is well known that the wise individual does not give up what he loves unless it is for something better. Hence, Allah reveals that the whoever is killed for His sake when fighting so that the word of Allah may be supreme and His religion may prevail, not for any other purpose, is not missing out on the life that he loves, rather, he has attained a life that is more perfect than what you may think or imagine. Al-Saadi: 75.\nWhen does a person give up what he loves?\nوَلَنَبۡلُوَنَّكُم بِشَيۡءٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡخَوۡفِ وَٱلۡجُوعِ وَنَقۡصٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡأَمۡوَٰلِ وَٱلۡأَنفُسِ وَٱلثَّمَرَٰتِۗ وَبَشِّرِ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ١٥٥\nIt is said that they were tested as a sign for those who come after them so that they know they were patient as truth was clear to them. Alternatively; It is said that Allah informed them of the coming test so that they would be certain that it would happen, be ready for it and become less likely to be anxious. Moreover, it advances Allah's reward for their resolve and preparation of the soul. Al-Qurtubi: 2/462.\nWhy does Allah inform His servants that they will be tested?\nوَلَنَبۡلُوَنَّكُم بِشَيۡءٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡخَوۡفِ وَٱلۡجُوعِ وَنَقۡصٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡأَمۡوَٰلِ وَٱلۡأَنفُسِ وَٱلثَّمَرَٰتِۗ\nIf times of ease were to persist for people of faith without any trials, then telling truth apart from falsehood would not be clear and that would lead to mischief. Allah's wisdom dictates that good people should be distinguished from others. The purpose of tests is not to cause the believers to lose their faith or turn away from the religion, for Allah will not let the faith of the believers go to waste. But in this verse, He reveals that He will test His servants (with some fear) of their enemies (and famine). Meaning: He will test them with a little of these things, because if He tested them with extensive fear or hunger, they would perish, but the purpose of tests is to purify, not to destroy. Al-Saadi: 76.\nWhy are people tested with some fear and famine, and not with all?\nٱلَّذِينَ إِذَآ أَصَٰبَتۡهُم مُّصِيبَةٞ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا لِلَّهِ وَإِنَّآ إِلَيۡهِ رَٰجِعُونَ ١٥٦\nThat is: Allah owns us and we are under His control; we have nothing of ourselves and our property at all. If He afflicts us with any of it, then the Most Merciful has decreed something concerning His servants and their property as He wills, so there should be no objection to Him. Al-Saadi: 76.\nIt is appropriate for someone who is afflicted with a calamity to say, (We belong to Allah). Why?\nٱلَّذِينَ إِذَآ أَصَٰبَتۡهُم مُّصِيبَةٞ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا لِلَّهِ وَإِنَّآ إِلَيۡهِ رَٰجِعُونَ ١٥٦\nWe belong to Allah), indicates ownership to Allah, and the owner does in His dominion what He Wills. (And to Him we will return), a reminder of the Hereafter to ease for them this life's afflictions. In the authentic hadith, Allah's Messenger (r) said: \"If any servant suffers a calamity and says: \"We belong to Allah and to Him we will return; O Allah, reward me for my affliction and replace it with something better,\" Allah will replace it with something better.\" Umm Salama said: \"When Abu Salama died, I said these words, and Allah replaced him with the Messenger of Allah (r).\" Ibn Juzay: 1/89.\nWhat is the recommended supplication to say when a calamity strikes?\nٱلَّذِينَ إِذَآ أَصَٰبَتۡهُم مُّصِيبَةٞ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا لِلَّهِ وَإِنَّآ إِلَيۡهِ رَٰجِعُونَ ١٥٦\nAllah made these words a refuge for those afflicted and a protection for those who are tested because of the blessed meanings they contain; namely, Tawhīd (Oneness of Allah), acknowledging His servitude, the resurrection from the graves, and entrusting all matters to Him as they belong to Him. Saeed bin Jubair (a prominent scholar) said: These words were not given to any prophet before our Prophet (r), and if Prophet Jacob (u) had known them, he would not have said: (Oh, my sorrow over Joseph). Ibn Atiyah: 1/228.\nWhat is the wisdom behind saying this supplication during calamities?\nwords\nيَلعَنُهُمُCursed them"],[25,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nChoose one of the creatures mentioned in this verse, then extract three features in it that are indicative of Allah's power and wisdom.\nExtract from the Quran three deeds that Allah Almighty loves, and do them today.\nWrite about a type of food that scholars have declared forbidden, but people have been lenient with it, along with a Fatwa from one of the scholars, and share it in a message with your acquaintances.\nguid\nIf the love for people exceeds its limit, it becomes \"shirk of love\"; do not exceed the limit in your love for them, no matter what their status is.\nFrequent remembrance of a loved one is indicative of a great love for him. The servant's frequent remembrance of his Lord (Allah) means that his love for his Lord is great.\nEating forbidden food is one the first luring steps of satan; as happened to our father Adam (u).\nrefl\nوَٱلۡفُلۡكِ ٱلَّتِي تَجۡرِي فِي ٱلۡبَحۡرِ بِمَا يَنفَعُ ٱلنَّاسَ\n(There are signs for people who use reason), the meaning of the sign in these great ships is that Allah controls them so that they move on the surface of the water and float despite their weight. Al-Qurtubi: 2/494.\nExplain the meaning of the sign with respect to great ships that sail in the sea.\nوَتَصۡرِيفِ ٱلرِّيَٰحِ وَٱلسَّحَابِ ٱلۡمُسَخَّرِ بَيۡنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ١٦٤\n(Directing of the winds), sending them from different directions -the four known directions and everything in between- and with different properties; winds that pollenate trees, barren winds, winds contain frost, winds to help the believers achieve victory in battles, and winds for destruction. Ibn Juzay: 1/91.\nDescribe the might and power of Allah in directing the types of winds.\nوَتَصۡرِيفِ ٱلرِّيَٰحِ وَٱلسَّحَابِ ٱلۡمُسَخَّرِ بَيۡنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ١٦٤\nIt is said that directing the winds means that sometimes winds are calm and in other times they become stormy; sometimes they are hot and in other times they are cold. Ibn Abbas said: \"The greatest soldiers of Allah are wind and water.\" Al-Baghawi: 1/132.\nWhat are the greatest soldiers of Allah?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَتَّخِذُ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ أَندَادٗا يُحِبُّونَهُمۡ كَحُبِّ ٱللَّهِۖ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ أَشَدُّ حُبّٗا لِّلَّهِۗ\nKnow that when the love of Allah becomes firm in the heart, its effects are reflected on the body, such as diligence in obeying Him, enthusiasm to serve Him, eagerness to please Him, delight in communing with Him, contentment with His decrees, longing to meet Him (in the Hereafter), comfort in remembering him, feeling lonely in the presence of others, avoiding people, preferring solitude, removing the love of worldly life from the heart, loving everyone loved by Allah and preferring them over others. Ibn Juzay: 1/92.\nWhat are the signs of a firm love in the heart?\nإِذۡ تَبَرَّأَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتُّبِعُواْ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُواْ وَرَأَوُاْ ٱلۡعَذَابَ وَتَقَطَّعَتۡ بِهِمُ ٱلۡأَسۡبَابُ ١٦٦\nThe disbelievers thought that the ones they followed had some power and that they could bring them closer to Allah. They will see that their assumptions are wrong, their efforts are in vain, and severe punishment is due to them, which their false gods cannot defend them or offer them the slightest help. Rather, harm will reach them because of these false gods, whereas they thought that they would benefit them. Those who were followed will disavow the followers, and any ties that existed between them in this world will be severed, because these ties were for the sake of something other than Allah and were not in accordance with the command of Allah. Al-Saadi: 80.\nWhat will be the position of those who were followed from their followers on the Day of Resurrection?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُواْ لَوۡ أَنَّ لَنَا كَرَّةٗ فَنَتَبَرَّأَ مِنۡهُمۡ كَمَا تَبَرَّءُواْ مِنَّاۗ كَذَٰلِكَ يُرِيهِمُ ٱللَّهُ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ حَسَرَٰتٍ عَلَيۡهِمۡۖ وَمَا هُم بِخَٰرِجِينَ مِنَ ٱلنَّارِ ١٦٧\nTheir deeds that they hoped would benefit them will turn into a source of anguish and remorse for them. Then the followers will wish that they could be returned to this world to disavow what they followed, give up associating others with Allah, and strive hard for the sake of Allah alone. Al-Saadi: 80.\nWhen will the disbelievrs and polytheists among the followers be convinced of the error of their actions?\nكَذَٰلِكَ يُرِيهِمُ ٱللَّهُ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ حَسَرَٰتٍ عَلَيۡهِمۡۖ وَمَا هُم بِخَٰرِجِينَ مِنَ ٱلنَّارِ ١٦٧\nAs-Suddi said: \"They will be shown Paradise in the Hereafter, and they will see their houses therein if they had obeyed Allah. These houses will be divided among the believers, and that is when they will feel anguished. Allah attributes these deeds to them because they were commanded to do them. Anguish is the highest degree of regret for something lost. Al-Qurtubi: 3/11.\nHow will the disbelievers reach the point of anguish on the Last Day?\nwords\nوَالفُلكِGreat ships\nوَبَثَّDisperses\nوَتَصرِيفِ الرِّيَاحِDirecting of the winds\nالأَسبَابُTies, Relationships\nحَسَرَاتٍAnguishes"],[26,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nSend a message reminding your brethren to avoid blind imitation and follow the authentic proof.\nOffer thanks to Allah after eating, as there are many who wish for the same food but cannot find it.\nShare a message with a list of names of questionable food items and another list of halal alternatives.\nguid\nThe believer is keen to follow the authentic proof from the Quran and Sunnah and does not follow those who speak without authentic proofs.\nOffering gratitude to Allah is an act of worship, therefore, maintain it.\nIt is a mercy from Allah that the basic principle regarding food is permissibility, while what is forbidden is limited to few items.\nrefl\nوَمَثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ كَمَثَلِ ٱلَّذِي يَنۡعِقُ بِمَا لَا يَسۡمَعُ إِلَّا دُعَآءٗ وَنِدَآءٗۚ صُمُّۢ بُكۡمٌ عُمۡيٞ فَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡقِلُونَ ١٧١\nBecause they are preoccupied with imitation and are attached to their misguidance, they do not pay attention to what is recited to them nor do they reflect on what is been explained to them. Therefore, they are like farm animals which hear only the rings of the bell and the cry of the voice. Al-Alusi: 2/42.\nWhy does Allah describe the disbelievers with such descriptions?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ كُلُواْ مِن طَيِّبَٰتِ مَا رَزَقۡنَٰكُمۡ وَٱشۡكُرُواْ لِلَّهِ إِن كُنتُمۡ إِيَّاهُ تَعۡبُدُونَ ١٧٢\nThe command to give thanks comes immediately after mentioning the blessings because gratitude preserves existing blessings and brings about missing ones, whereas ingratitude repels blessings that are missing and causes existing ones to be lost. Al-Saadi: 81.\nWhat is the link between gratitude and blessings?\nوَٱشۡكُرُواْ لِلَّهِ إِن كُنتُمۡ إِيَّاهُ تَعۡبُدُونَ ١٧٢\nThe true meaning of gratitude is giving of good things. Offering gratitude for each blessing is to show it in its proper form, whether it is wealth, status, knowledge, food or drinks or other things, spend the excess of it, and be content with its minimum. Those who wish to receive Allah's reward trade with Him by giving the excess of the blessings to the needy since they are entrusted with these blessings, as the treasuries of the Generous King (Allah) come to pass at the hands of His servants. Al-Biqai: 1/316.\nWhat is the true meaning of gratitude?\nإِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡمَيۡتَةَ وَٱلدَّمَ وَلَحۡمَ ٱلۡخِنزِيرِ وَمَآ أُهِلَّ بِهِۦ لِغَيۡرِ ٱللَّهِۖ فَمَنِ ٱضۡطُرَّ غَيۡرَ بَاغٖ وَلَا عَادٖ فَلَآ إِثۡمَ عَلَيۡهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٌ ١٧٣\nSince Islam is a religion of ease not hardship, blame or burden, these forbidden food items can be consumed by one who is compelled by necessity. Al-Biqai: 1/318.\nIslamic Sharia is valid for all times and places because it takes into account all conditions. Explain in light of this verse.\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَكۡتُمُونَ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَيَشۡتَرُونَ بِهِۦ ثَمَنٗا قَلِيلًا أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ مَا يَأۡكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمۡ إِلَّا ٱلنَّارَ وَلَا يُكَلِّمُهُمُ ٱللَّهُ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ وَلَا يُزَكِّيهِمۡ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ ١٧٤\n(Nor will He purify them), as He will purify whomever He Wills of His servants. They will not be purified since they have concealed knowledge that purifies others. This highlights the enormity of this sin. (And they will have) along with this punishment (A painful punishment) for causing people a great difficulty by concealing knowledge that would guide them on to the straight path. Al-Biqai: 1/320.\nWhy is purification denied to those who conceal what Allah has revealed?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَكۡتُمُونَ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَيَشۡتَرُونَ بِهِۦ ثَمَنٗا قَلِيلًا أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ مَا يَأۡكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمۡ إِلَّا ٱلنَّارَ\nAllah calls it (small) because it is short-lived, and incurs terrible consequence. Moreover, it is said that the amounts of bribes they used to take were small. Even though this verse describes Jewish scholars, nevertheless, it is applicable to some Muslims who conceal the truth for the sake of worldly gains. The use of the word (bellies) alludes to their greed and the fact that they have sold the Hereafter for a portion of food that had no value. Al-Qurtubi: 3/48-49\nWho is generally meant by this verse? What is the significance of the phrase \"in their bellies\"?\nفَمَآ أَصۡبَرَهُمۡ عَلَى ٱلنَّارِ ١٧٥\nMeaning: How persistent they are in continuing to commit sins that will lead them to Hellfire. Ibn Kathir: 1/196.\nThey are described as patient even though they have not entered the Fire yet. How?\nwords\nيَنعِقُCries (when calling)\nأُهِلَّ بِهِ لِغَيرِ اللَّهِAn animal which has been sacrificed to other than Allah\nغَيرَ بَاغٍNot driven by desire\nوَلاَ عَادٍNot exceeding the permissible limit\nشِقَاقٍ بَعِيدٍExtreme dissension"],[27,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nMake a schedule for distributing your charity and gifts of what you love to those who are listed in the verse.\nGo early to prayer.\nStart drafting your will with the help of an experienced consultant.\nguid\nLearn about some deeds of the heart, then determine how to attain them.\nThe believer fulfills his pledge and never breaches it; only a hypocrite breaks a pledge.\nLegal retribution promotes stability and safety of societies.\nrefl\nوَءَاتَى ٱلۡمَالَ عَلَىٰ حُبِّهِۦ ذَوِي ٱلۡقُرۡبَىٰ وَٱلۡيَتَٰمَىٰ وَٱلۡمَسَٰكِينَ وَٱبۡنَ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَٱلسَّآئِلِينَ وَفِي ٱلرِّقَابِ\n(Relatives) and what follows in this verse are arranged in order of priority based on importance, because charity given to relatives is charity and a bond of kinship, unlike those who come after them. The (orphans) come next due to their young age and need. Then, comes (the needy) for their poverty; (the traveler) who is a stranger or weak, and (those who ask for help) even if they are not in real need. Ibn Juzay: 1/95.\nThe verse focuses on priorities and what is most important. Explain.\nوَءَاتَى ٱلۡمَالَ عَلَىٰ حُبِّهِۦ\nWhen a person gives of his wealth, despite his love for it, in order to draw closer to Allah, it is proof of his faith. Part of giving one's wealth despite his love for it is to give charity when one is healthy and inclined to be stingy, hoping for wealth and fearing poverty. Similarly, giving charity when one does not have much is better, since in this case he loves to keep it because of what is expected of need and poverty. Likewise, giving for charity out of the precious part of one's wealth, and what he loves most. Al-Saadi: 83.\nState some examples of giving wealth despite one's love for it.\nوَأَقَامَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَى ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَٱلۡمُوفُونَ بِعَهۡدِهِمۡ إِذَا عَٰهَدُواْۖ وَٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ فِي ٱلۡبَأۡسَآءِ وَٱلضَّرَّآءِ وَحِينَ ٱلۡبَأۡسِۗ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ صَدَقُواْۖ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُتَّقُونَ ١٧٧\nThat is: Those who are characterized by these qualities are truthful in their faith because they have realized the faith in their hearts in words and deeds. Hence, they are the truthful and righteous ones since they avoided prohibitions and performed acts of obedience. Ibn Kathir: 1/198.\nWhat is the sign of true faith?\nوَٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ فِي ٱلۡبَأۡسَآءِ وَٱلضَّرَّآءِ وَحِينَ ٱلۡبَأۡسِۗ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ صَدَقُواْۖ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُتَّقُونَ ١٧٧\nSituations for which patience is required are listed in ascending order based on the degree of hardship. Patience in sickness exceeds patience in poverty, while patience in battle fields exceeds patience in sickness. Al-Alusi: 2/48.\nDo degrees of patience vary?\nفَمَنۡ عُفِيَ لَهُۥ مِنۡ أَخِيهِ شَيۡءٞ فَٱتِّبَاعُۢ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَأَدَآءٌ إِلَيۡهِ بِإِحۡسَٰنٖۗ\nAllah recommends that the pardoner to be lenient when requesting blood money and allows the pardoned person more time if he is insolvent. Moreover, it is recommended that the pardoned not to delay the pardoner's payment or reduce the agreed upon amount, and to pay it when possible. Al-Alusi: 2/50.\nWhat does Allah command both parties to do when taking blood money or pardon?\nوَلَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡقِصَاصِ حَيَوٰةٞ يَٰٓأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَّقُونَ ١٧٩\n(And in the legal retribution, there is saving of life for you), similar in meaning to the famous Arabic saying, \"Killing negates further killing.\" legal retribution deters people from further killings because it is killing one person for one person, unlike what was done in the pre-Islamic period where if a person was killed, his tribe fought against the killer's tribe until a group of people were killed because of it. Ibn Juzay: 1/96.\nHow can legal retribution save lives?\nفَمَنۢ بَدَّلَهُۥ بَعۡدَ مَا سَمِعَهُ فَإِنَّمَآ إِثۡمُهُ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ يُبَدِّلُونَهُۥٓۚ\nWhoever changes the will or alters it by addition or deletion -including concealment of the will- then (the sin is upon those who have altered it). Ibn Abbas and others said, \" The reward for the deceased is preserved for him by Allah, while the sin is upon those who changed the will.\" Ibn Kathir: 1/201.\nChoosing a good executer of the will is important. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nالبِرَّDoing good deeds extensively\nوَابنَ السَّبِيلِA traveler who is in need\nوَفِي الرِّقَابِFor freeing slaves\nالبَأسَاءِPoverty\nوَالضَّرَّاءِSickness\nوَحِينَ البَأسِHard fighting in battles\nتَرَكَ خَيرًاLeaves wealth"],[28,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nReconcile today between two people who are in conflict or debt, while being aware of the importance of reconciliation.\nFast three days out of each month to attain righteousness of the heart.\nDetermine a major goal you hope for in your life, then fast a day and supplicate Allah fervently for it, while being certain that He will respond to your supplication.\nguid\nOne of the benefits of fasting is helping and training oneself to attain righteousness.\nFasting, whether obligatory or optional, has many benefits to the believer, whether he knows them or not.\nGuidance and direction can be achieved through supplication.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ كُتِبَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلصِّيَامُ كَمَا كُتِبَ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَّقُونَ ١٨٣ أَيَّامٗا مَّعۡدُودَٰتٖۚ\nThe intended meaning behind saying: (As it was decreed upon those before you) and (a limited number of days), is to ease fasting for Muslims with gentle comforting words. Ibn Juzay: 1/95.\nIn His Sharia, Allah combines wisdom and mercy. Explain in light of this verse.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ كُتِبَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلصِّيَامُ كَمَا كُتِبَ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ\nThis is because fasting is one of the laws and commands that are of interest to creation at all times, and it is an encouragement to this nation (Muslims) that they should compete with others in perfecting deeds and hastening to good qualities, and that it is not one of the burdens that they have been singled out for. Al-Saadi: 86.\nKnowing that fasting was decreed upon those before us is beneficial. Explain.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ كُتِبَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلصِّيَامُ كَمَا كُتِبَ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَّقُونَ ١٨٣\nMeaning: So that you avoid sins, because fasting inhibits lustful desires. The Prophet (r) said: \"O young men, whoever among you can afford it, let him get married, for it is more effective in lowering the gaze and guarding one's chastity, and whoever cannot afford it, let him fast, as it will be a restraint for him.\" Al-Alusi: 2/57.\nHow does fasting lead to righteousness?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ كُتِبَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلصِّيَامُ كَمَا كُتِبَ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَّقُونَ ١٨٣\nAllah, the Almighty, says, \"Every deed of the son of Adam is his except for fasting, it is Mine and I reward for it.\" Even though all acts of worship are in fact His, Allah singles out fasting as being His for two reasons that make fasting different from other acts of worship. First: Fasting curtails lustful desires in a way that all other acts of worship do not except prayer. Second: Fasting is a secret between the servant and his Lord, and is only revealed to Him . All other acts of worship are outward and may contain some artifice and showing off, which is not the case with fasting. That is why fasting is specially for Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 3/123.\nExplain the virtues of fasting over other forms of worship.\nوَلِتُكۡمِلُواْ ٱلۡعِدَّةَ وَلِتُكَبِّرُواْ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ مَا هَدَىٰكُمۡ\nSince Eid is a time of joy and pleasure, and it is in the nature of the soul to exceed the limits due to its nature of gluttony -sometimes out of negligence or transgression- Allah commands Muslims to repeat saying: \"Allah Akbar\" (Allah is the Greatest). Al-Biqai: 1/345.\nAllah Commands Muslims to repeat saying, \"Allah Akbar\" starting on the night before the day of Eid. Why?\nوَإِذَا سَأَلَكَ عِبَادِي عَنِّي فَإِنِّي قَرِيبٌۖ أُجِيبُ دَعۡوَةَ ٱلدَّاعِ إِذَا دَعَانِۖ\nIn this verse, Allah mentions that He is Near and responds to the call of supplicant. In another verse, He explained that this is conditional upon His will, (And He would remove that for which you invoked Him if He willed, and you would forget what you associate with Him) [6:41]. Some said that the conditional response is to the supplications of the disbelievers, as is apparent in the context of the verse, while the absolute response is to the supplications of the believers. Accordingly, their supplication will not be rejected; either they will be given what they asked for, or saving for them something better, or averting evil from them. Al-Shanqiti: 1/74.\nWhat is the difference between the supplication of a believer and that of a disbeliever with respect to the response from Allah?\nوَإِذَا سَأَلَكَ عِبَادِي عَنِّي فَإِنِّي قَرِيبٌۖ أُجِيبُ دَعۡوَةَ ٱلدَّاعِ إِذَا دَعَانِۖ فَلۡيَسۡتَجِيبُواْ لِي وَلۡيُؤۡمِنُواْ بِي لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَرۡشُدُونَ ١٨٦\nThis verse indicates that the supplication of a fasting person is answered, the supplications during the month of Ramadan are answered, and that supplication should be made at the end of each day of the month of Ramadan. Ibn Ashur: 2/179.\nWhat is the wisdom behind including the verse of supplication between the verses of fasting?\nwords\nجَنَفًاPartiality by mistake or ignorance\nتَطَوَّعَ خَيرًاOne who volunteers to give more\nفَليَستَجِيبُوا لِيLet them obey Me\nيَرشُدُونَThey are guided"],[29,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nList five harmful effects of bribery on the individual and society, and share them in a message.\nCooperate with others to recover the right of a Muslim that was taken due to bribery.\nRecall a Muslim you have wronged and apologize to him, even through a message, so that Allah will love you.\nguid\nThe purpose of sending down laws and setting limits is to make people righteous.\nDo not approach suspicious matters, lest you fall into forbidden ones.\nBeware of consuming people's wealth unjustly.\nrefl\nوَكُلُواْ وَٱشۡرَبُواْ حَتَّىٰ يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكُمُ ٱلۡخَيۡطُ ٱلۡأَبۡيَضُ مِنَ ٱلۡخَيۡطِ ٱلۡأَسۡوَدِ مِنَ ٱلۡفَجۡرِۖ\nAllah's permission to eat and drink until dawn proves that Suhur (pre-dawn meal) is desirable, and Allah likes His permissions to be exercised. Ibn Kathir: 1/310.\nHow can we infer from this verse that Suhur is desirable?\nوَلَا تُبَٰشِرُوهُنَّ وَأَنتُمۡ عَٰكِفُونَ فِي ٱلۡمَسَٰجِدِۗ\nBy mentioning I'tikaf (devotional retreat) after fasting, Allah draws attention to practicing I'tikaf during the month of fasting (Ramadan), especially during the last part of the month. Ibn Kathir: 1/213.\nWhat is inferred from mentioning I’tikaf after fasting?\nوَلَا تُبَٰشِرُوهُنَّ وَأَنتُمۡ عَٰكِفُونَ فِي ٱلۡمَسَٰجِدِۗ\nI'tikaf (devotional retreat) can only be performed in mosques, as unanimously agreed by scholars, as Allah says, (Should you be in a devotional retreat in the mosques then do not be intimate with them). I'tikaf cannot be performed in solitude, nor in a cave or at a grave site as it is done by misguided people who travel to devote themselves to grave sites, similar to what polytheists did with their idols. Ibn Taimyah: 1/448.\nIs it permissible to perform I'tikaf outside of mosques? Extract evidence from the verse.\nتِلۡكَ حُدُودُ ٱللَّهِ فَلَا تَقۡرَبُوهَاۗ\nAllah says, (So do not approach them), which is more eloquent than saying \"do not do them\", because the prohibition of going near them includes the prohibition of doing the forbidden actions themselves and the prohibition of the means that lead to it. Al-Saadi: 87-88.\nWhy is the term (approach) used and not \"do\"?\nوَلَا تَأۡكُلُوٓاْ أَمۡوَٰلَكُم بَيۡنَكُم بِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ وَتُدۡلُواْ بِهَآ إِلَى ٱلۡحُكَّامِ لِتَأۡكُلُواْ فَرِيقٗا مِّنۡ أَمۡوَٰلِ ٱلنَّاسِ بِٱلۡإِثۡمِ وَأَنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ١٨٨\nAfter Allah mentions fasting and what it entails, He warns against unlawful consumption of people's wealth that leads to the non-acceptance of one's worship, including his fasting and I’tikaf. Al-Alusi: 2/69.\nWhat is the link between fasting and prohibition of unlawful consumption?\nوَلَا تَأۡكُلُوٓاْ أَمۡوَٰلَكُم بَيۡنَكُم بِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ وَتُدۡلُواْ بِهَآ إِلَى ٱلۡحُكَّامِ لِتَأۡكُلُواْ فَرِيقٗا مِّنۡ أَمۡوَٰلِ ٱلنَّاسِ بِٱلۡإِثۡمِ وَأَنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ١٨٨\nDo not bribe judges with your wealth to make them rule in your favor. Scholars of Ahl As-Sunnah agree that whoever accepts any kind of wealth -little or much- in this way becomes defiantly disobedient, and this wealth is forbidden for him to take. Al-Qurtubi: 3/226.\nPreserving one's fasting is to keep away from bribery. Explain.\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ١٨٩\nWhoever fears Allah, the springs of wisdom flow from his heart, and ambiguous matters will become apparent to him commensurate with his level of righteousness. Al-Alusi: 2/74.\nWhat is the fruit of righteousness?\nwords\nالرَّفَثُSexual relation\nلِبَاسٌShield from forbidden acts\nتَختَانُونَCommit a sin\nبَاشِرُوهُنَّHave intimacy with them\nحُدُودُ اللَّهِProhibitions\nوَتُدلُواPay"],[30,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nGive a gift to the family of someone who is dedicated to serve Islam.\nDo good today to a poor or a disabled person, for Allah loves that from you.\nPut a financial and time plan, even if takes a long time, to save money for performing Hajj or Umrah.\nguid\nSpending in the way of Allah is a security for individuals and society while holding back on spending leads to destruction.\nBe proficient in doing your charitable work to gain the love of Allah.\nBe mindful of your sincerity in worshiping Allah.\nrefl\nوَٱلۡفِتۡنَةُ أَشَدُّ مِنَ ٱلۡقَتۡلِۚ\nMeaning: Persecuting a believer to turn him away from his faith is worse than killing him. It is said that the disbelief of disbelievers is worse than the believers killing them in battlefield. Ibn Juzay: 1/100.\nHow can we infer from the above verse that preserving religion is the most important objective of Sharia?\nوَٱلۡفِتۡنَةُ أَشَدُّ مِنَ ٱلۡقَتۡلِۚ\nSince Jihad involves loss of lives and killing of men, Allah points out that what these disbelievers are involved in of disbelief in Allah, polytheism, and turning people away from His path is more severe, more terrible, and worse than killing. For this reason, Allah says, (And fitnah is worse than killing). Ibn Kathir: 1/215-216.\nWhat is meant by \"fitnah\"? What is meant by \"killing\"? Which is more severe?\nوَقَٰتِلُوهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ لَا تَكُونَ فِتۡنَةٞ وَيَكُونَ ٱلدِّينُ لِلَّهِۖ\nAllah states the purpose of fighting in His cause; it is not to shed the blood of disbelievers and take their wealth; rather, the aim is to make worship devoted to Allah alone in order that the religion of Allah may prevail over all other religions, and to ward off everything that is opposed to it, such as polytheism and other things. Al-Saadi: 89.\nThis verse establishes the true aim for fighting the disbelievers, and clarifies misconceptions that are held by many people about this subject. Explain.\nفَمَنِ ٱعۡتَدَىٰ عَلَيۡكُمۡ فَٱعۡتَدُواْ عَلَيۡهِ بِمِثۡلِ مَا ٱعۡتَدَىٰ عَلَيۡكُمۡۚ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ\nWhen people are given permission for retribution, they often would not stop at the prescribed limits due to their desires for vengeance; therefore, Allah commands to always fear Him, which is to stop at His limits and not transgress them. Al-Saadi: 90.\nAllah commands fearing Him when repelling aggression. Why?\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ ١٩٤\nSince fearing Allah often goes against self-interests, Allah let them know that He will be their compensation for their own selves because of what they feared and persevered in piety until it became a characteristic of them, and informs them that He is with them. Al-Biqai: 1/367.\nWhat is the reason for Allah's company of those who fear Him?\nوَأَنفِقُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَلَا تُلۡقُواْ بِأَيۡدِيكُمۡ إِلَى ٱلتَّهۡلُكَةِ\nAbu Ayyub (t) said: This verse was revealed about us, a group of the Ansar. When Allah strengthened His religion and granted victory to His Messenger (r), we said among ourselves, \"We had left our families and our wealth until Islam spread and Allah granted victory to His Prophet (r). So let us return to our families and wealth and stay in them and repair what was lost of them.\" Thereupon Allah, the Exalted, revealed, (And Spend in the way of Allah and do not throw yourselves into destruction). Throwing oneself into destruction means staying in one's property and family and abandon Jihad. Al-Baghawi: 1/171.\nWhat is meant by throwing oneself into destruction?\nوَأَنفِقُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَلَا تُلۡقُواْ بِأَيۡدِيكُمۡ إِلَى ٱلتَّهۡلُكَةِ وَأَحۡسِنُوٓاْۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ١٩٥\nSince spending is an essential element in supporting Jihad and life in the early days of Islam was difficult and money was scarce, this was a reason for everyone to hold on to what he had, thinking that in holding on to it he would survive, and in spending it he would perish, then Allah clarifies that what they were doing was in fact their destruction because satan threatens them with poverty while Allah promises them a great bounty, (satan threatens you with poverty) [2-268]. Al-Biqai: 1/367.\nWhen the call to Jihad is made, what is the way to salvation? And what is the way to destruction?\nwords\nثَقِفتُمُوهُمWhere you found them\nوَالفِتنَةُ\"Persecution of Muslims or \"shirk\nوَلاَ تُلقُوا بِأَيدِيكُمDo not throw yourselves\nالتَّهلُكَةِSelf-Destruction by abandoning Jihad and unwilling to spend for it\nأُحصِرتُمObstructed by sickness or enemy\nالهَديِAn animal gifted to Ka'ba\nنُسُكٍA slaughtered sheep to be given to the needy in Makkah\nحَاضِرِيResidents of Makkah"],[31,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nPut a financial and time plan to save money so you can reach financial independence while making sure that your effort does not distract you from your religious duties.\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness after each completed act of worship or a good deed acknowledging your shortcomings, and make that a habit of yours.\nToday, repeat this supplication more often\nguid\nThose who are aware of the aims of the acts of worship have better understanding and higher morals.\nAttend to things that mend your heart just like you take care of what you eat and drink.\nDo not belittle any good deed even if it is small, for it may be great in the sight of Allah.\nrefl\nٱلۡحَجُّ أَشۡهُرٞ مَّعۡلُومَٰتٞۚ فَمَن فَرَضَ فِيهِنَّ ٱلۡحَجَّ فَلَا رَفَثَ وَلَا فُسُوقَ وَلَا جِدَالَ فِي ٱلۡحَجِّۗ\nAlhasan said: \"The accepted Hajj is when a person returns ascetic of this world and eager for the Hereafter.\" Al-Qurtubi: 3/324\nWhat is the sign of an accepted Hajj?\nفَلَا رَفَثَ وَلَا فُسُوقَ وَلَا جِدَالَ فِي ٱلۡحَجِّۗ وَمَا تَفۡعَلُواْ مِنۡ خَيۡرٖ يَعۡلَمۡهُ ٱللَّهُۗ\nEncouraging and urging good speech instead of obscenity, and righteousness and piety in morals instead of immorality and argumentation. Al-Qurtubi: 3/328.\nExplain the Holy Quran's emphasis on kind words and avoiding offensive speech.\nوَتَزَوَّدُواْ فَإِنَّ خَيۡرَ ٱلزَّادِ ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰۖ وَٱتَّقُونِ يَٰٓأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ١٩٧\nAllah specifically addresses those with understanding, for they have good judgement and can distinguish between truth and falsehood. They have the right thought and knowledge that enable them to see the reality of things that are perceived by the mind and understood by the heart. Those who are ignorant are not addressed by this verse. Al-Tabari: 4/161.\nAllah commands only the people of understanding to fear Him. Why?\nوَتَزَوَّدُواْ فَإِنَّ خَيۡرَ ٱلزَّادِ ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰۖ وَٱتَّقُونِ يَٰٓأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ١٩٧\nThis verse was revealed about a group of people who went for Hajj without carrying the necessary food and money for the journey, and some of them said: We rely upon Allah. Others said: How is it possible that we visit the House of Allah while He does not feed us? They would remain dependent on people, so they were forbidden from doing so and were ordered to prepare provisions. Ibn Atiyah: 1/273.\nNeglecting to take the necessary means to reach an end is not considered reliance upon Allah. Explain.\nلَيۡسَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ جُنَاحٌ أَن تَبۡتَغُواْ فَضۡلٗا مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡۚ\nWhen Allah prohibits arguing during Hajj, people may presume that this prohibition includes trading also since doing business normally entails arguing, so Allah states the ruling on trading. Al-Alusi: 2/87.\nAllah Almighty permits trade during Hajj after forbidding arguing? Why?\nفَإِذَا قَضَيۡتُم مَّنَٰسِكَكُمۡ فَٱذۡكُرُواْ ٱللَّهَ كَذِكۡرِكُمۡ ءَابَآءَكُمۡ أَوۡ أَشَدَّ ذِكۡرٗاۗ فَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَقُولُ رَبَّنَآ ءَاتِنَا\nAllah combines Thikr (Remembrance of Him) with supplication to indicate that only Thikr with attentive heart is considered, as is the case of the supplicant when he asks for a need, not just the mere utterance of the words. Allah starts with Thikr because it is the key to the answer for supplication, then He mentions those whose love of this world overcomes them, so they only supplicate for it, and those who supplicate Him for the goodness of this world and the Hereafter. Al-Alusi: 2/90.\nAllah combines Thikr (Remembrance of Him) with supplication. Why? And why does He start with Thikr?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ نَصِيبٞ مِّمَّا كَسَبُواْۚ وَٱللَّهُ سَرِيعُ ٱلۡحِسَابِ ٢٠٢\nAli Bin Abi Talib (t) was asked: \"How will Allah hold people accountable on the Day of Judgment despite their large numbers?\" He said, \"Just as He provides for them despite their large numbers.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/103.\nHow will Allah hold people accountable on the Day of Judgement?\nwords\nأَشهُرٌ مَعلُومَاتٌThe months of Hajj are: Shawwal, Thu al-Qa'dah and ten days of Thu al-Ḥijjah\nرَفَثَSexual intercourse\nفَضلًاProfiting from trading\nأَفَضتُم مِن عَرَفَاتٍReturning from the valley of Arafat after sunset"],[32,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nOur evaluation of others falls between two extremes. Consult with those around you to write down rules for evaluating others.\nIdentify a contemporary person who you think has sold himself to seek Allah's pleasure, and reflect on his life.\nRecall a repeated sin of yours, and determine the footsteps of satan in leading you to it so that you become cautious of his first steps.\nguid\nArrogance prevents one from accepting advice, therefore, seek refuge with Allah from it frequently, and warn others against it.\nBe one of those who sell themselves and their time seeking the pleasure of Allah and hoping for His Paradise.\nBeware of the devil and his evil whispers, and remember that he uses footsteps to lure the believer into sin; therefore, seek refuge with Allah from him often.\nrefl\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يُعۡجِبُكَ قَوۡلُهُۥ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَيُشۡهِدُ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ مَا فِي قَلۡبِهِۦ وَهُوَ أَلَدُّ ٱلۡخِصَامِ ٢٠٤\nThis verse indicates that intense quarrel is despicable; the Prophet (r) said: \"The most despicable amongst people in the sight of Allah is the one who quarrels most.\" Intense quarrel is a trait of hypocrites because of their attachment to worldly things. Al-Alusi: 2/95\nDisputes are permissible but intense quarrels are censured. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يُعۡجِبُكَ قَوۡلُهُۥ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَيُشۡهِدُ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ مَا فِي قَلۡبِهِۦ وَهُوَ أَلَدُّ ٱلۡخِصَامِ ٢٠٤ وَإِذَا تَوَلَّىٰ سَعَىٰ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ لِيُفۡسِدَ فِيهَا وَيُهۡلِكَ ٱلۡحَرۡثَ وَٱلنَّسۡلَۚ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡفَسَادَ ٢٠٥\nIn this verse there is evidence that the statements made by people are not evidence of truth or falsehood, righteousness or immorality unless there are actions that confirm that. Therefore, witnesses and those who are right or wrong among people should all be verified by examining their deeds, and looking at the evidence of their conditions. One should not be deceived by how they present or praise themselves. Al-Saadi: 94.\nWhat is the true test of the credibility of people's words? ?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يُعۡجِبُكَ قَوۡلُهُۥ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَيُشۡهِدُ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ مَا فِي قَلۡبِهِۦ وَهُوَ أَلَدُّ ٱلۡخِصَامِ ٢٠٤\nThis verse contains evidence and a warning to be cautious regarding matters of religion and the world, and the need to verify the conditions of witnesses and judges, and that the ruler/judge should not base his judgment merely on the outward appearance of people or any display of faith and righteousness without investigating their inward conditions, because Allah reveals the conditions of people where some make good talk while intend evil. Al-Qurtubi: 3/383.\nMany of our mistakes are due to misjudging others, and this verse warns against that. Explain.\nوَإِذَا تَوَلَّىٰ سَعَىٰ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ لِيُفۡسِدَ فِيهَا وَيُهۡلِكَ ٱلۡحَرۡثَ وَٱلنَّسۡلَۚ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡفَسَادَ ٢٠٥\n(And when he goes away), when he leaves those whom he deceived with his words, (he strives), walks throughout the land to cause corruption by casting doubts in the hearts of Muslims, and devising tricks to strengthen disbelief. Al-Qasimi: 1/82.\nIt is wise to link man's words to his actions. Explain in light of this verse.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱدۡخُلُواْ فِي ٱلسِّلۡمِ كَآفَّةٗ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُواْ خُطُوَٰتِ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِۚ\n(Enter into Islam completely): that is, adhere to all teachings of Islam and do not neglect any of them. Do not be among those who take their desires as their god, and follow Allah's command only when it is in line with their whims, otherwise they do not. Rather, the right thing to do is to make one's desires subordinate to Sharia's teachings, and perform as much good deeds as he is able to. Al-Saadi: 94.\nWhy are we commanded to enter into Islam completely?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱدۡخُلُواْ فِي ٱلسِّلۡمِ كَآفَّةٗ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُواْ خُطُوَٰتِ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِۚ\nSince entering into Islam completely is only possible and conceivable by opposing the ways of satan, Allah says: (And do not follow the footsteps of satan). Al-Saadi: 94.\nAfter Allah commands us to enter Islam completely, He forbids us from following the footsteps of satan. Why?\nفَإِن زَلَلۡتُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَتۡكُمُ ٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتُ فَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ ٢٠٩\nThe verse proves that the punishment of one for a sin of which he is aware is greater than that of another who is ignorant of it. Al-Qurtubi: 3/395.\nThe obedience of a knowledgeable person is greater than that of an ignorant one, and so is his disobedience. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nأَلَدُّ الخِصَامِIntense in animosity\nفَحَسبُهُAdequate for him\nالمِهَادُResting place\nظُلَلٍ مِنَ الغَمَامِCovers of clouds"],[33,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you explain that women displaying their allurements is an examples of ingratitude for Allah's favors.\nThank Allah for revealing and preserving the Holy Quran, for it has preserved Islam from distortion and alteration that happened to other religions.\nVisit a Muslim who has been afflicted with a trial, and remind him that only a believer is afflicted, and that the consequence of affliction is Paradise.\nguid\nSteadfastness in faith, values and principles is a shield for individuals and society.\nThe beginning of the nation's failure and its exposure to loss and destruction is when its people dispute over its book and religion, out of desires and whims, in pursuit of leadership and authority.\nWarning against the tyranny of the love of worldly adornments and their dominance over the heart.\nrefl\nسَلۡ بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ كَمۡ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُم مِّنۡ ءَايَةِۢ بَيِّنَةٖۗ وَمَن يُبَدِّلۡ نِعۡمَةَ ٱللَّهِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَتۡهُ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ ٢١١\nThe essence of this substitution is rejecting the knowledge of the scholar by not becoming guided by it, and rejecting the righteousness of the righteous by not following his example. Al-Biqai: 1/390.\nWhat is the essence of the substitution mentioned in the verse?\nوَمَن يُبَدِّلۡ نِعۡمَةَ ٱللَّهِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَتۡهُ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ ٢١١\nIf Allah bestows a blessing, either religious or worldly, upon a person who does not give thanks for it or does what is required of him as a result, then this blessing will diminish and disappear, and it will be replaced with disbelief and sin. Thus, disbelief becomes a substitute for the blessing. As for the one who gives thanks to Allah and does what is required of him, the blessing will remain and continue, and Allah will increase it for him. Al-Saadi: 95.\nHow do blessings continue? And how do they cease?\nزُيِّنَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَيَسۡخَرُونَ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْۘ وَٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوۡاْ فَوۡقَهُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۗ\nThey ridiculed the believers who followed you because they abstained from competition in wealth and leaderships and boasting about them, and concerned themselves only with Allah's bounty by abandoned worldly adornments. Al-Tabari: 4/273.\nWhat are the standards of the people of this world for success and prosperity?\nفَهَدَى ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لِمَا ٱخۡتَلَفُواْ فِيهِ مِنَ ٱلۡحَقِّ بِإِذۡنِهِۦۗ وَٱللَّهُ يَهۡدِي مَن يَشَآءُ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٍ ٢١٣\nAisha (i) said that when the Prophet (r) stood up to pray at night, he began his prayer by saying: \"O Allah, Lord of Gabriel, Mikael and Israfil, Creator of the heavens and Earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, You judge between Your servants in that which they differ. Guide me to the truth by Your leave in what they have differed, for verily You guide whom You will to a straight path.\" Ibn Taimyah: 1/493.\nThe Prophet (r) used to seek guidance from Allah in matters of disagreement, so what was his supplication?\nأَمۡ حَسِبۡتُمۡ أَن تَدۡخُلُواْ ٱلۡجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَأۡتِكُم مَّثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ خَلَوۡاْ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۖ مَّسَّتۡهُمُ ٱلۡبَأۡسَآءُ وَٱلضَّرَّآءُ وَزُلۡزِلُواْ حَتَّىٰ يَقُولَ ٱلرَّسُولُ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مَعَهُۥ مَتَىٰ نَصۡرُ ٱللَّهِۗ أَلَآ إِنَّ نَصۡرَ ٱللَّهِ قَرِيبٞ ٢١٤\n(Or do you think): Addressing the believers to encourage them to be patient when facing hardships. (Without being tested), means that you will not enter Paradise until you are afflicted with what befell the people before you. Ibn Juzay: 1/107.\nIn light of this verse, what is the condition for entering Paradise?\nأَمۡ حَسِبۡتُمۡ أَن تَدۡخُلُواْ ٱلۡجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَأۡتِكُم مَّثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ خَلَوۡاْ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۖ مَّسَّتۡهُمُ ٱلۡبَأۡسَآءُ وَٱلضَّرَّآءُ وَزُلۡزِلُواْ حَتَّىٰ يَقُولَ ٱلرَّسُولُ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مَعَهُۥ مَتَىٰ نَصۡرُ ٱللَّهِۗ أَلَآ إِنَّ نَصۡرَ ٱللَّهِ قَرِيبٞ ٢١٤\nA declaration from Allah that He relieves the distress of His Prophets and those with them only after they severed all ties to everyone but Him in order to test their hearts for righteousness, and their consciences become attached to Him, the Almighty, alone. Al-Biqai: 1/397.\nWhy is victory delayed sometimes? Explain in light of this verse.\nيَسۡٔلُونَكَ مَاذَا يُنفِقُونَۖ قُلۡ مَآ أَنفَقۡتُم مِّنۡ خَيۡرٖ فَلِلۡوَٰلِدَيۡنِ وَٱلۡأَقۡرَبِينَ وَٱلۡيَتَٰمَىٰ وَٱلۡمَسَٰكِينِ وَٱبۡنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِۗ وَمَا تَفۡعَلُواْ مِنۡ خَيۡرٖ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِهِۦ عَلِيمٞ ٢١٥\nThe verse is concluded by asserting that Allah is All-Knowing of one's spending because boasting and showing off is part of human nature. Al-Biqai: 1/400.\nWhat is the significance of concluding this verse with Allah's attribute of knowledge?\nwords\nالبَأسَاءُPoverty\nوَالضَّرَّاءُIllness"],[34,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nRecall a thing you hoped to attain but did not, and another that you disliked but it occurred, and thank Allah in both cases, for it was good for you.\nWrite down three benefits from this great verse.\nRepeat this supplication today: \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm on Your religion.\"\nguid\nJihad in the cause of Allah is a law that will continue until the Last Day.\nA sincere Muslim submits to Allah's command, even if it goes against his desires.\nThe main reason for waging war against Muslim countries is religion, no matter how the warring disbelievers tried to disguise it.\nrefl\nكُتِبَ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡقِتَالُ وَهُوَ كُرۡهٞ لَّكُمۡۖ وَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تَكۡرَهُواْ شَيۡٔاً وَهُوَ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡۖ وَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تُحِبُّواْ شَيۡٔاً وَهُوَ شَرّٞ لَّكُمۡۚ\nThis dislike is due to the natural aversion to war because of its difficulties and risks to wealth and souls; it is not because they disliked the command of Allah. Al-Baghawi: 1/203.\nHow can fighting in the cause of Allah be disliked by the believers?\nوَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تَكۡرَهُواْ شَيۡٔاً وَهُوَ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡۖ\nFighting is good for you because it is followed by victory and triumph over the enemies, and the seizure of their lands, money and offspring. Ibn Kathir: 1/239.\nHow can fighting be good even though it appears to cause pain and difficulties?\nوَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تُحِبُّواْ شَيۡٔاً وَهُوَ شَرّٞ لَّكُمۡۚ\nAbstaining from fighting may lead the enemy to seize control of the Muslim country and the government. Ibn Kathir: 1/239.\nThe society may rejoice in abandoning fighting, but that would be bad for it. How so?\nيَسۡٔلُونَكَ عَنِ ٱلشَّهۡرِ ٱلۡحَرَامِ قِتَالٖ فِيهِۖ قُلۡ قِتَالٞ فِيهِ كَبِيرٞۚ وَصَدٌّ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَكُفۡرُۢ بِهِۦ وَٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِ وَإِخۡرَاجُ أَهۡلِهِۦ مِنۡهُ أَكۡبَرُ عِندَ ٱللَّهِۚ وَٱلۡفِتۡنَةُ أَكۡبَرُ مِنَ ٱلۡقَتۡلِۗ\nIf killing during the Sacred Months is evil, then persecution of Muslims by the disbelievers and prevailing of disbelief is far greater evil than killing, so the greater evil is warded off by committing to the lesser of the two. Ibn Taimyah: 1/501.\nWhich action is more harmful: leading society to disbelief, or leading it to Jihad?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَٱلَّذِينَ هَاجَرُواْ وَجَٰهَدُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يَرۡجُونَ رَحۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِۚ\nAn indication that even if a servant performs as many deeds as he has done, he should not rely on them, but rather hope for the mercy of his Lord, hope for acceptance of his deeds, forgiveness of his sins, and concealment of his imperfections. Al-Saadi: 98.\nThis verse contains great guidance for those who do good deeds. What is it?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَٱلَّذِينَ هَاجَرُواْ وَجَٰهَدُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يَرۡجُونَ رَحۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٢١٨\nAfter Allah praised them, He says, (they who hope), because no one in this world knows if he will enter Paradise even if he reaches every level in obedience to Allah, for two reasons: One of them is that he does not know what will happen to him, and the second is so that he does not rely on his deeds. Al-Qurtubi: 3/432.\nWhy is the word (they who hope) used even though the believers had maintained great deeds?\nكَذَٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٢١٩\nReflecting on these verses revealed by Allah so you may infer its laws and benefits for the public good, as it helps you choose what is best for you and evade what is harmful. Al-Alusi: 2/116.\nWhat are the benefits of reflecting on the verses of the Holy Quran?\nwords\nوَالفِتنَةُShirk, Associating partners with Allah\nوَالمَيسِرِGambling"],[35,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nBe kind to an orphan, or help sponsor him.\nThere are advocates of good and advocates of evil In every society. Identify the advocates of good, support them and pray for them.\nRenew your ablution today for every prayer, even if you do not have to.\nguid\nAsking trustworthy people about the rulings on money and preserving rights is a characteristic of the righteous and successful.\nAllah's command to the believer is to look for a believing wife.\nIslam is the religion of cleanliness and purity, as the Holy Quran clarifies all details about how to be clean and pure.\nrefl\nوَلَا تَنكِحُواْ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكَٰتِ حَتَّىٰ يُؤۡمِنَّۚ وَلَأَمَةٞ مُّؤۡمِنَةٌ خَيۡرٞ مِّن مُّشۡرِكَةٖ وَلَوۡ أَعۡجَبَتۡكُمۡۗ وَلَا تُنكِحُواْ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ حَتَّىٰ يُؤۡمِنُواْۚ وَلَعَبۡدٞ مُّؤۡمِنٌ خَيۡرٞ مِّن مُّشۡرِكٖ وَلَوۡ أَعۡجَبَكُمۡۗ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يَدۡعُونَ إِلَى ٱلنَّارِۖ\n(They invite unto the fire), means: By their words, deeds and attitude, so mixing with them poses a risk, not in worldly terms, but in terms of eternal doom. What we learn from this verse is that it is not allowed to mix with polytheists and the misguided, because if it is not permissible to marry them, even though doing so may serve many interests, then it is more appropriate to say that mixing with them in a regular manner is not allowed, especially in cases where a polytheist is in a higher position than the Muslim. Al-Saadi: 99.\nHow do we infer from this verse the risk of mixing with the misguided and polytheists?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يَدۡعُونَ إِلَى ٱلنَّارِۖ وَٱللَّهُ يَدۡعُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱلۡجَنَّةِ وَٱلۡمَغۡفِرَةِ بِإِذۡنِهِۦۖ وَيُبَيِّنُ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٢٢١\nThe intended meaning is that the believer should be cautious of what will harm him in the Hereafter, and should steer clear of any possibility of being in harm's way even though human nature and the devil push one into the direction of Hellfire. Al-Alusi: 2/120.\nWhen is a Muslim more likely to be in harm's way?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحِبُّ ٱلتَّوَّٰبِينَ وَيُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُتَطَهِّرِينَ ٢٢٢\nThis verse consoles those who repeatedly fall into sin after repenting over and again; when going through that, they may fear being considered as liars and unworthy in the sight of Allah, and that may stop them from repenting. Al-Biqai: 1/422.\nThe phrase \"repentant\" which means continuity is used in this verse. Why?\nوَبَشِّرِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٢٢٣\n(And give glad tidings to the believers). There is no mention of what the glad tidings are about in order to indicate the general meaning, and that they will have glad tidings in this world and the Hereafter. Attaining all that is good and being protected from all that is evil as a consequence of their faith are included in these glad tidings. Al-Saadi: 100.\nWhy is there no mention of what the glad tidings are about?\nوَلَا تَجۡعَلُواْ ٱللَّهَ عُرۡضَةٗ لِّأَيۡمَٰنِكُمۡ\nMeaning: Take fewer oaths by Allah to maintain His fear in your hearts. That is why Allah says, (Keep your oaths) [5:89], and He censured those who swear oaths excessively: (Do not obey any vile swearer of oaths) [68:10]. Al-Qurtubi: 4/13.\nWhat is the benefit of taking fewer oaths?\nوَلَا تَجۡعَلُواْ ٱللَّهَ عُرۡضَةٗ لِّأَيۡمَٰنِكُمۡ أَن تَبَرُّواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ وَتُصۡلِحُواْ بَيۡنَ ٱلنَّاسِۚ وَٱللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٞ ٢٢٤\nAllah forbade them from making the oath by Him a deterrent to doing what He commanded, lest they refrain from obeying Him with the oath they swore. Ibn Taimyah: 1/517.\nWhen is taking oath censured?\nوَلَا تَجۡعَلُواْ ٱللَّهَ عُرۡضَةٗ لِّأَيۡمَٰنِكُمۡ أَن تَبَرُّواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ وَتُصۡلِحُواْ بَيۡنَ ٱلنَّاسِۚ وَٱللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٞ ٢٢٤\nThen the verse concludes with these two noble names: (And Allah is All-Hearing) He hears all sounds. (All-Knowing) He knows people's aims and intentions. That includes His hearing of the words of those who swear oaths, and His knowledge of their intentions, whether they are good or evil. This is a warning that He will requite them for their deeds, and He has full knowledge of their actions and their intentions. Al-Saadi: 100-101.\nThe verse concludes with emphasis on the importance of swearing an oath. Explain.\nwords\nلأَعنَتَكُمHe could have put you in difficulty\nحَرثٌ لَكُمYour wives are meant for you to cultivate (sowing of seed)\nأَنَّىCome to your place of cultivation however you wish\nعُرضَةًHindrance"],[36,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nGlorify Allah by not swearing an oath today.\nBuy a gift today and present it to your wife; or give it to your father so he can present it to your mother in his name.\nShare a message warning against distorting women's rights and using them as a pretext to corrupt them by hypocrites and those who are deceived by their approach.\nguid\nbenefit of the waiting period is for the married couple to contemplate their feelings and interests before the divorce becomes final.\nThe family will prosper when the rights and duties of each spouse are fulfilled.\nShare a message warning against distorting women's rights and using them as a pretext to corrupt them by hypocrites and those who are deceived by their approach.\nrefl\nلَّا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِٱللَّغۡوِ فِيٓ أَيۡمَٰنِكُمۡ وَلَٰكِن يُؤَاخِذُكُم بِمَا كَسَبَتۡ قُلُوبُكُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٞ ٢٢٥\nSharia laws do not hold one accountable except for what the heart earns of outward words and actions, as Allah says, (but He holds you accountable for what your hearts have intended). A person is not held responsible for words or deeds of which the heart is not aware, nor intends. Likewise, what a person tells himself, he will not be held accountable for except for what he said or did. Ibn Taimyah: 1/517.\nWhen is a person held accountable for his actions? Explain in light of the verse.\nلَّا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِٱللَّغۡوِ فِيٓ أَيۡمَٰنِكُمۡ وَلَٰكِن يُؤَاخِذُكُم بِمَا كَسَبَتۡ قُلُوبُكُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٞ ٢٢٥\nAllah does not hasten to punish His servants. Forbearing means the tolerance of the higher toward annoyance of the lower. Al-Biqai: 1/426.\nThis verse concludes with the attribute of Allah: The Most Forbearing. Why?\nوَلَهُنَّ مِثۡلُ ٱلَّذِي عَلَيۡهِنَّ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِۚ وَلِلرِّجَالِ عَلَيۡهِنَّ دَرَجَةٞۗ\nIbn Abbas (t) said: I like to adorn myself for my wife just as she likes to adorn herself for me because Allah says, (Women have rights similar to the rights over them in a reasonable manner). Al-Baghawi: 1/225.\nSharia law does not only aim to eliminate the causes of divorce, but also to create happiness between spouses. Explain.\nوَلَهُنَّ مِثۡلُ ٱلَّذِي عَلَيۡهِنَّ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِۚ وَلِلرِّجَالِ عَلَيۡهِنَّ دَرَجَةٞۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ ٢٢٨\nMarital rights between spouses are not determined by the marriage contract, but by common tradition, as evidenced by the Holy Quran (Women have rights similar to the rights over them in a reasonable manner). Ibn Taimyah: 1/523.\nWhat is the basis for marital rights between spouses?\nوَلِلرِّجَالِ عَلَيۡهِنَّ دَرَجَةٞۗ\nThe advantage of men over women is not oblivious to any rational individual, as women were created from men and that make them their origin. A wife needs her husband's consent before fasting or performing Hajj. Al-Qurtubi: 4/53.\nDisbelievers and hypocrites call for a blind equality between men and women. How do you answer them?\nٱلطَّلَٰقُ مَرَّتَانِۖ\nSince any one who does it more than twice is either daring to do something forbidden, or has no desire to keep her, but rather his intention is to cause harm. Al-Saadi: 102.\nWhy is the revocable divorce limited to two only?\nفَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيۡهِمَآ أَن يَتَرَاجَعَآ إِن ظَنَّآ أَن يُقِيمَا حُدُودَ ٱللَّهِۗ\nThis indicates that if a person wants to do something, especially holding a public position of major or minor responsibility, he should first assess himself; If he is confident that he has the ability to carry out the responsibility, then, he should go ahead, otherwise he should refrain. Al-Saadi: 103.\nHow should a person deal with offers to hold public positions?\nwords\nبِاللَّغوِ فِي أیمانکMaking unintentional oaths\nيُؤلُونَFor those who swear not to have intercourse with their wives\nتَرَبُّصُRemain in waiting\nففاؤواThe husbands return to normal relations\nيَتَرَبَّصنَThe wives should remain in waiting\nثَلاَثَةَ قُرُوءٍThree menstrual periods"],[37,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you explain that whoever tampers with the rules of marriage, will tamper with the rules of divorce, and this is mocking the rulings of Allah.\nIn the morning, say, \"O Allah, in this morning whatever blessing has been received by me or anyone of Your creation is from You alone, You have no partner. All praise and thanks are to You.\" In the evening, say, \"O Allah, in this evening...\".\nEncourage the guardians of a quarreling or divorced couple to facilitate their reconciliation.\nguid\nA decent honorable man treats his wife with nothing but kindness whether he likes her or not.\nAnger and disputes do not justify mocking Sharia laws.\nAccept the advice and admonition even from a humble source, and reflect on it because that affirms your faith in Allah and the Last Day.\nrefl\nوَلَا تَتَّخِذُوٓاْ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ هُزُوٗاۚ\n(Do not take the verses of Allah in jest): By turning away from them and being lax in keeping with them, but rather take them seriously, apply and observe them with due observance. Al-Alusi: 2/143.\nTampering with the rules of marriage leads to tampering with the rules of divorce and ridiculing Sharia laws. Explain.\nوَلَا تَتَّخِذُوٓاْ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ هُزُوٗاۚ\nMocking the religion of Allah in jest is considered a major sin. Mockery is ridicule and interpreting words and actions as jest and play. Ibn Taimyah: 1/543.\nWhat is the ruling on mocking the religion of Allah?\nوَإِذَا طَلَّقۡتُمُ ٱلنِّسَآءَ فَبَلَغۡنَ أَجَلَهُنَّ فَلَا تَعۡضُلُوهُنَّ أَن يَنكِحۡنَ أَزۡوَٰجَهُنَّ إِذَا تَرَٰضَوۡاْ بَيۡنَهُم بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِۗ\nThis verse was revealed about a man who divorces his wife once or twice and when her waiting period ends, he decides to take her back in marriage. The woman also wants to do that, but her guardians prevent her from remarrying him. Hence, Allah forbade them from preventing her. This indicates that a woman is not permitted to give herself in marriage. Rather, marriage requires the presence of a guardian such as her father, brother, adult son, and so forth. Ibn Kathir: 1/267.\nHow does this verse support the requirement of a male guardian for a woman in marriage?\nوَإِذَا طَلَّقۡتُمُ ٱلنِّسَآءَ فَبَلَغۡنَ أَجَلَهُنَّ فَلَا تَعۡضُلُوهُنَّ أَن يَنكِحۡنَ أَزۡوَٰجَهُنَّ إِذَا تَرَٰضَوۡاْ بَيۡنَهُم بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِۗ ذَٰلِكَ يُوعَظُ بِهِۦ مَن كَانَ مِنكُمۡ يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِۗ ذَٰلِكُمۡ أَزۡكَىٰ لَكُمۡ وَأَطۡهَرُۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَعۡلَمُ وَأَنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٢٣٢\n(This is better and purer): This refers to allowing divorced women to get back with their former husbands. It is better for their souls and purer for their faith and honor, and to evade potential relations between them in the future to which the guardian is oblivious. Preventing them to get back with their husbands can lead to unlawful mixing and corruption, and Allah knows what people do not. Ibn Atiyah: 1/310.\nWhen does the involvement of a third party in marital matters harm them?\nذَٰلِكَ يُوعَظُ بِهِۦ مَن كَانَ مِنكُمۡ يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِۗ\nThe verse indicates that this advice is not easily recognized by everyone, so there must be guidance from Allah. (This [advice] is an admonition for all among you who believe in Allah and the Last Day), they are mentioned because they are the ones who hasten to comply out of reverence for Allah, the Almighty, and fear of His punishment. Al-Alusi: 2/145.\nThis advice is directed to the believer in Allah and the Last Day. Why?\nوَٱلۡوَٰلِدَٰتُ يُرۡضِعۡنَ أَوۡلَٰدَهُنَّ حَوۡلَيۡنِ كَامِلَيۡنِۖ لِمَنۡ أَرَادَ أَن يُتِمَّ ٱلرَّضَاعَةَۚ\n(Two full years): This indicates that the completed period for breastfeeding is two years, and anything beyond that is food. Ibn Taimyah: 1/553.\nWhat is the completed period for breastfeeding?\nلَا تُضَآرَّ وَٰلِدَةُۢ بِوَلَدِهَا وَلَا مَوۡلُودٞ لَّهُۥ بِوَلَدِهِۦۚ وَعَلَى ٱلۡوَارِثِ مِثۡلُ ذَٰلِكَۗ\nThe mother should not refuse to breastfeed her baby in order to harm the father, or to ask for more than her wage. It is not permissible for the father to prevent the mother from breastfeeding the baby when she wants to. Al-Qurtubi: 4/116.\nHow can the mother and father cause harm to each other in the matter of breastfeeding their baby?\nwords\nضِرَارًاIntending harm\nتَعضُلُوهُنَّPreventing the women from remarrying their former husbands\nفِصَالًاWeaning"],[38,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nToday, train yourself to think only of doing good deeds, whether you are alone or when mixing with others.\nRepent to Allah from a secret sin.\nRemember someone who has wronged you, and forgive him, hoping that your Lord will compensate you with piety in your heart.\nguid\nSurrendering to evil thoughts is the beginning of sin, so repel them as much as you can.\nMake your dealings with people based on kindness and benevolence toward them.\nIslam recommends preserving past kindness and favor of people , as this is more likely to lead to forgiving their present shortcomings.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوۡنَ مِنكُمۡ وَيَذَرُونَ أَزۡوَٰجٗا يَتَرَبَّصۡنَ بِأَنفُسِهِنَّ أَرۡبَعَةَ أَشۡهُرٖ وَعَشۡرٗاۖ\nMourning is when a widow abandons all adornment, including clothing, perfume, jewelry, eyeliner, and henna, as long as she is in her waiting period, because adornment is an invitation to husbands, so she is forbidden from that in order to block the means and protect the sanctities of Allah Almighty from being violated. Al-Qurtubi: 4/133.\nExplain the wisdom behind the mourning of widows.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوۡنَ مِنكُمۡ وَيَذَرُونَ أَزۡوَٰجٗا يَتَرَبَّصۡنَ بِأَنفُسِهِنَّ أَرۡبَعَةَ أَشۡهُرٖ وَعَشۡرٗاۖ\nSaeed bin Al-Musayib said: The reason for this time period is because it is the time during which the life is breathed into the fetus. It was said that the fetus starts moving in the womb. Al-Baghawi: 1/238.\nExplain the wisdom behind specifying the mourning period to be four months and ten days?\nفَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ فِيمَا فَعَلۡنَ فِيٓ أَنفُسِهِنَّ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِۗ\nThis proves that the guardian looks after the woman, and that he should prevent her from doing what is not permissible as well as force her to do what is obligatory; this is addressed to him and it is his duty. Al-Saadi: 105.\nWhat is the duty of the guardian toward the woman?\nلَّا جُنَاحَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ إِن طَلَّقۡتُمُ ٱلنِّسَآءَ مَا لَمۡ تَمَسُّوهُنَّ أَوۡ تَفۡرِضُواْ لَهُنَّ فَرِيضَةٗۚ وَمَتِّعُوهُنَّ عَلَى ٱلۡمُوسِعِ قَدَرُهُۥ وَعَلَى ٱلۡمُقۡتِرِ قَدَرُهُۥ مَتَٰعَۢا بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِۖ\nAllah allows divorce after the marriage contract and before consummating the marriage, even though this may break her heart. Therefore, Allah commands the husband to give her a gift of a reasonable amount -the rich according to his means and the poor according to his means- to compensate her for her loss. Ibn Kathir: 1/272.\nAllah commands that a divorced woman who has not been consummated with be given a compensation. Why?\nوَأَن تَعۡفُوٓاْ أَقۡرَبُ لِلتَّقۡوَىٰۚ وَلَا تَنسَوُاْ ٱلۡفَضۡلَ بَيۡنَكُمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ ٢٣٧\nPeople deal with each other on two levels: Either in justice and fairness, which is obligatory, and is the basis on which people give and take what is due, or in graciousness and kindness, which means giving what is not due and being easygoing with regard to one's own rights, suppressing any feelings of annoyance. No one should forget this level, even if it occurs in some occasions. Al-Saadi: 105.\nWe are forbidden from forgetting graciousness between us. What does that mean?\nوَلَا تَنسَوُاْ ٱلۡفَضۡلَ بَيۡنَكُمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ ٢٣٧\nGraciousness means kindness, which means: Do not forget the kindness that existed between you before [as couple]. Let it be remembered by you so that each one of you will desire forgiveness in return for the kindness of his companion towards him. Al-Alusi: 3/155.\nWhy are the couple asked to remember the graciousness that was between them?\nوَلَا تَنسَوُاْ ٱلۡفَضۡلَ بَيۡنَكُمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ ٢٣٧\nSince the man has a higher degree of responsibility, he should be the one who forgives. The woman was not addressed nor encouraged to do that. The most unpleasant thing that can happen is for the man to force the woman to give back what he had given her (as a dowery); therefore, do not forget the kindness between you. Al-Biqai: 1/448.\nWhat can we infer from this verse: (And do not forget graciousness between you)?\nwords\nعَرَّضتُمAllude concerning a proposal for marriage\nأَكنَنتُمConcealed in your hearts\nعُقدَةَ النِّكَاحِMarriage contract\nتَفرِضُواDetermine\nفَرِيضَةًA dowery\nوَمَتِّعُوهُنَّGive them some money as consolation"],[39,"§Al-Baqarah, Al-An'am\ndeeds\nGo early to Al-Asr prayer.\nReflect on the images of those who prostrate before shrines and idols, sacrifice to them, and stroll around them, then thank Allah for the blessing of guidance.\nLend your Lord a good loan, for you will need it greatly when the time comes for payback.\nguid\nMentioning the verse on prayer among the verses of divorce proves that maintaining prayer in the family is an important factor in its stability and happiness.\nMaintain with care all daily prayers on time, especially Al-Asr prayer.\nTaking all precautions do not change fate, however, it is important to submit to Allah's Will while adopting means to reach your objectives.\nrefl\nحَٰفِظُواْ عَلَى ٱلصَّلَوَٰتِ وَٱلصَّلَوٰةِ ٱلۡوُسۡطَىٰ وَقُومُواْ لِلَّهِ قَٰنِتِينَ ٢٣٨\nAllah will give one a share of this life if his intention is directed toward the Hereafter, but will He will not give him a share of the Hereafter if his intention is directed to this life. The defect in a person's condition in this world and the Hereafter is due to a flaw in his religion. The foundation of his religion and faith is his prayers, therefore, if he maintains the prayers, Allah will mend his life in this world and the Hereafter. Al-Biqai: 1/450.\nMentioning the verse on prayer among the verses of divorce indicates a link between family well-being and prayer. What is this link?\nحَٰفِظُواْ عَلَى ٱلصَّلَوَٰتِ وَٱلصَّلَوٰةِ ٱلۡوُسۡطَىٰ وَقُومُواْ لِلَّهِ قَٰنِتِينَ ٢٣٨\nSome scholars said: The middle prayer is not a particular one but it is one of the five daily prayers. Allah concealed it in order to encourage the believers to continue to maintain all prayers, just as He concealed the Night of Al-Qadr in the month of Ramadan, the hour of answering supplications on Fridays, and His greatest Name so that the believers would maintain all of them. Al-Baghawi: 1/252.\nSometimes the virtue of worship is mentioned but the specific act of worship is not specified, what is the wisdom of this?\nفَإِنۡ خِفۡتُمۡ فَرِجَالًا أَوۡ رُكۡبَانٗاۖ\nThis implies that this may be done whether one is facing the Qiblah or not; this further emphasizes the importance of offering prayer on time, as this is enjoined even if it means omitting some of the essential parts or conditions, or not doing them. It is not permissible to delay the prayer until after the time for it has ended even in these extreme circumstances. Performing the prayer in that [imperfect] manner is better and preferable, and even more obligatory than offering it in safety and calm manner outside its prescribed time. Al-Saadi: 106.\nWhat does the command to pray, whether walking or riding, in case of fear indicate?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ خَرَجُواْ مِن دِيَٰرِهِمۡ وَهُمۡ أُلُوفٌ حَذَرَ ٱلۡمَوۡتِ فَقَالَ لَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ مُوتُواْ ثُمَّ أَحۡيَٰهُمۡۚ\nThe purpose of this noble verse is to encourage the believers to fight their enemies by informing them that fleeing from death does not really save them. If a person knows that his decision to avoid death or being killed will not save him, then it will be easy for him to hit the battlefield and confront the enemy. Al-Shanqiti: 1/152.\nWhat is the purpose of this verse?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ خَرَجُواْ مِن دِيَٰرِهِمۡ وَهُمۡ أُلُوفٌ حَذَرَ ٱلۡمَوۡتِ فَقَالَ لَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ مُوتُواْ ثُمَّ أَحۡيَٰهُمۡۚ\nAllah mentions this story to encourage Muslims to wage Jihad and be exposed to martyrdom. He urges them to rely on Him and be submissive to His Will as a prelude to commanding them in the next verse: (And fight in the cause of Allah). Al-Alusi: 2/162.\nAllah mentions this story before commanding the believers to fight their enemies. Why?\nمَّن ذَا ٱلَّذِي يُقۡرِضُ ٱللَّهَ قَرۡضًا حَسَنٗا فَيُضَٰعِفَهُۥ لَهُۥٓ أَضۡعَافٗا كَثِيرَةٗۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَقۡبِضُ وَيَبۡصُۜطُ وَإِلَيۡهِ تُرۡجَعُونَ ٢٤٥\n(A goodly loan): Giving a loan with kindness and for the sake of Allah. Abdullah Ibn Al-Mubarak said: Giving from halal money. Moreover, it was said: Giving without harming or considering it a favor. Al-Baghawi: 1/252.\nHow can a loan become a goodly one?\nمَّن ذَا ٱلَّذِي يُقۡرِضُ ٱللَّهَ قَرۡضًا حَسَنٗا\nA question that is intended to encourage the believers to spend their money. The term (loan) is used to bring closer to their minds that they should expect a reward just as the lender expects its return. Ibn Juzay: 1/118.\nWhat can we infer from using the term (loan) to encourage spending?\nwords\nوَالصَّلاَةِ الوُسطَىAl-Asr prayer\nخَوضِهِمTheir meaningless discourse\nقَانِتِينَDevoutly obedient\nفَرِجَالًاWalking"],[40,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nDo not wish to meet the enemy, and if you do meet him, be patient and steadfast.\nAsk Allah to make you one of His chosen ones in this world and the hereafter.\nSupplicate Allah much today by saying, \"My Lord increase my knowledge.\"\nguid\nSteadfastness in times of trial is one of the attributes of believers.\nAllah may choose from His servants scholars, preachers, worshipers, poor people, merchants and kings, so do not be envious of any of them.\nBeware of aspiring to positions of responsibility to please yourself, for it is a trial, but when you find yourself in one, seek Allah's help and get closer to Him.\nrefl\nقَالُواْ وَمَا لَنَآ أَلَّا نُقَٰتِلَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَقَدۡ أُخۡرِجۡنَا مِن دِيَٰرِنَا وَأَبۡنَآئِنَاۖ فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡقِتَالُ تَوَلَّوۡاْ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا مِّنۡهُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمُۢ بِٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٢٤٦\nThe lesson here is to warn against falling into the same situation as theirs after starting the fight or when it was enjoined upon them. Ibn Ashur: 2/484.\nWhat is the lesson here?\nقَالُواْ وَمَا لَنَآ أَلَّا نُقَٰتِلَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَقَدۡ أُخۡرِجۡنَا مِن دِيَٰرِنَا وَأَبۡنَآئِنَاۖ فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡقِتَالُ تَوَلَّوۡاْ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا مِّنۡهُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمُۢ بِٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٢٤٦\nA reminder to the Muslim nation not to initiate war, but rather to defend its right to establish Islam, as Allah said: (Permission [to fight] is given to those who are fought because they were oppressed), [22:39]. It is the right of the believer to refuse war and not pursue it, because if he does and is given the command to fight, he may turn away just as these Israelites did except for few of them. Al-Biqai: 1/470.\nPrimarily, we should always start by calling others to Islam, however, when does Jihad become obligatory?\nقَالُواْ وَمَا لَنَآ أَلَّا نُقَٰتِلَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَقَدۡ أُخۡرِجۡنَا مِن دِيَٰرِنَا وَأَبۡنَآئِنَاۖ\nAllah, the Almighty, reveals that they attributed their will to fight to their own anger at being expelled. Only those who fight in the cause of Allah fight so that His word is the highest throughout the land. Al-Biqai: 1/472.\nOne of the reasons that Allah abandons a fighter is his insincerity. Explain.\nفَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡقِتَالُ تَوَلَّوۡاْ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا مِّنۡهُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمُۢ بِٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٢٤٦\nWhen fighting was enjoined upon them and they saw the truth and their thoughts went to facing the war, they (turned away), meaning that their intentions became distorted and their resolve weakened. This is the nature of nations living in luxury and inclined toward ease, they wish for war but when they face it, they yield to their nature, and turn away from war. Ibn Atiyah: 1/331.\nWhat is the risk to a society leading a luxurious way of life?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱصۡطَفَىٰهُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ وَزَادَهُۥ بَسۡطَةٗ فِي ٱلۡعِلۡمِ وَٱلۡجِسۡمِۖ\nThat is: He is more perfect in knowledge and stature than you. Hence, the king should have knowledge, a good appearance, and great strength in his body and soul. Ibn Kathir: 1/285.\nThis verse contains some attributes that a king should have. What are they?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱصۡطَفَىٰهُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ وَزَادَهُۥ بَسۡطَةٗ فِي ٱلۡعِلۡمِ وَٱلۡجِسۡمِۖ\nThe increase in knowledge is mentioned before the increase in physique because mental virtues have far greater value than physical ones. In fact, there is almost no comparison between the two. Al-Alusi: 2/167.\nWhy is the increase in knowledge mentioned before the increase in physique?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱصۡطَفَىٰهُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ وَزَادَهُۥ بَسۡطَةٗ فِي ٱلۡعِلۡمِ وَٱلۡجِسۡمِۖ\nMeaning: Do not rule out his kingship over you due to his poverty and low lineage. That is because: First: The whole matter rests on Allah's selection, and He chose him since Allah Knows what is best for you. Second: The basis for this choice is knowledge so he can handle the governing issues, and a good physique so he can be a strong leader in war against your enemies. Al-Alusi: 2/167.\nWhen selecting the right people, what is the difference between divine standards and human ones?\nwords\nهَل عَسَيتُمHow likely is it\nبَسطَةًAbundance\nالتَّابُوتُThe Ark of the Torah"],[41,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nRead the story of Saul from a reference on the interpretations of the Holy Quran, then draw three useful lessons.\nAsk Allah to make you steadfast in faith, then practice your patience by fasting a day so you will be firm during times of trials and tribulation.\nSupplicate Allah, and advise others who are in tribulation.\nguid\nAllah is the One Who pours forth patience, and sets firm the feet and gives victory over the disbelievers.\nSupplicating Allah during times of trials and showing your need of Him is the most important factor for achieving victory at war.\nLong reflection about the Hereafter brings about steadfastness and certainty in Allah and His victory.\nrefl\nقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَظُنُّونَ أَنَّهُم مُّلَٰقُواْ ٱللَّهِ كَم مِّن فِئَةٖ قَلِيلَةٍ غَلَبَتۡ فِئَةٗ كَثِيرَةَۢ بِإِذۡنِ ٱللَّهِۗ وَٱللَّهُ مَعَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ٢٤٩\nThis verse encourages fighting, detects patience, and presents a path to follow the example of those who are true to Allah. This is how we must act, but evil actions and false intentions have prevented that until the many of us are defeated by a small enemy, as we have witnessed many times, and we have brought that on ourselves! Abu-Darda' said: \"You only fight by your deeds.\" Al-Qurtubi: 4/245.\nThis verse mentions a reason for victory over the enemy. What is it?\nوَٱللَّهُ مَعَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ٢٤٩\nThe patience of the servant is the greatest means for seeking Allah's help. Al-Saadi: 108.\nWhat is the greatest means for seeking Allah's help?\nوَلَمَّا بَرَزُواْ لِجَالُوتَ وَجُنُودِهِۦ قَالُواْ رَبَّنَآ أَفۡرِغۡ عَلَيۡنَا صَبۡرٗا وَثَبِّتۡ أَقۡدَامَنَا وَٱنصُرۡنَا عَلَى ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٢٥٠\nTheir supplication has the right order of requests, first: They asked for pouring of patience upon their hearts when encountering the enemy. Second: They asked to make their feet strong and firm on the ground, as patience alone may be attained by those who have no resistance. Third: They asked for the main objective of any conflict, which is victory over the enemy. Al-Alusi: 2/172.\nThe best supplication is the most inclusive of one's needs. Explain.\nفَهَزَمُوهُم بِإِذۡنِ ٱللَّهِ\nA wise person who admits his lack of knowledge and believes in the limitless power of his Lord should not entrust anything to his own power because it is, in fact, helpless, even if it claims otherwise. He should disown his power and strength in favor of the power and strength of his Lord, and should not cease asking Him for forgiveness and protection. Al-Biqai: 1/483.\nWhat is a good confidence and what is a bad one?\nوَقَتَلَ دَاوُۥدُ جَالُوتَ وَءَاتَىٰهُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمُلۡكَ وَٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ وَعَلَّمَهُۥ مِمَّا يَشَآءُۗ\nThis confirms the importance of having a ruler (king), without which world affairs would not be stable. Hence; it was said that religion and ruler are twins; when one rises the other does too, because religion is a foundation and the ruler is a guard. A building without foundation is a destroyed, and one without a guard is lost. Al-Alusi: 2/174.\nFrom this verse, explain the importance of having a ruler (king).\nوَلَوۡلَا دَفۡعُ ٱللَّهِ ٱلنَّاسَ بَعۡضَهُم بِبَعۡضٖ لَّفَسَدَتِ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ\nIn this verse, Allah states that if it were not for Him repelling the disbelievers by the believers throughout history, (the earth would be filled with corruption) because disbelief would have prevailed and persisted in all its regions, but Allah protects and provides for those who uphold the truth, call others to Him, and fight in His cause, until Allah has set the nation of Muhammad (r) to carry out this endeavor until the Last Day, so all praise be to Him. Ibn Atiyah: 1/337.\nAllah made the repel between the believers and disbelievers continued until the Last Day. Why?\nوَلَٰكِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ذُو فَضۡلٍ عَلَى ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢٥١\n(Allah is All-Gracious to the worlds), first: By creating them. Second: By repelling the transgression of the wrongdoers either by other wrongdoers or by righteous people -and they are few- and He amply bestows upon them His favors both apparent and hidden. Al-Biqai: 1/481.\nExplain some of Allah's graciousness to the worlds?\nwords\nيَظُنُّونَThose who are certain"],[42,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nGive to charity today -even if it is small- that will plead for you with Allah on this day\nRecite Ayat Al-Kursi after prescribed prayers, for only death is between you and entering Paradise.\nRecite Ayat Al-Kursi regularly in the morning and evening and before going to sleep so that Allah protects you from the devil.\nguid\nA reason for fighting is disagreement that stems from whims and ignorance.\nNothing will benefit a servant on the Day of Resurrection except his good deeds, the greatest of which is charity.\nYour constant awareness that Allah is watchful over you in private and in public will help you avoid committing sins.\nrefl\nتِلۡكَ ٱلرُّسُلُ فَضَّلۡنَا بَعۡضَهُمۡ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٖۘ مِّنۡهُم مَّن كَلَّمَ ٱللَّهُۖ وَرَفَعَ بَعۡضَهُمۡ دَرَجَٰتٖۚ\nIt is known that some Messengers exceed others in aspects such as: The books revealed to them, miracles proving their truthfulness, their Sharias (knowledge and practice), and the nations to whom they were sent. Ibn Taimyah: 1/578-579.\nState few aspects in which some of the Messengers of Allah exceed others.\nوَٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ هُمُ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ ٢٥٤\nAṭa' bin Dinar said, \"Praise be to Allah who says: (And the disbelievers - they are the wrongdoers), and does not say that the wrongdoers are the disbelievers.\" Al-Qurtubi: 4/262.\nExplain how Ata' bin Dinar reflected on the meaning of this verse.\nٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ٱلۡحَيُّ ٱلۡقَيُّومُۚ لَا تَأۡخُذُهُۥ سِنَةٞ وَلَا نَوۡمٞۚ\nAllah Almighty rules out being overtaken by sleep since it is considered a deficiency while He is impeccable and free from all deficiencies and faults. Al-Baghawi: 1/269.\nAllah Almighty rules out being overtaken by sleep. Why?\nٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ٱلۡحَيُّ ٱلۡقَيُّومُۚ لَا تَأۡخُذُهُۥ سِنَةٞ وَلَا نَوۡمٞۚ لَّهُۥ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۗ مَن ذَا ٱلَّذِي يَشۡفَعُ عِندَهُۥٓ إِلَّا بِإِذۡنِهِۦۚ يَعۡلَمُ مَا بَيۡنَ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَمَا خَلۡفَهُمۡۖ وَلَا يُحِيطُونَ بِشَيۡءٖ مِّنۡ عِلۡمِهِۦٓ إِلَّا بِمَا شَآءَۚ وَسِعَ كُرۡسِيُّهُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَۖ وَلَا ئَودُهُۥ حِفۡظُهُمَاۚ وَهُوَ ٱلۡعَلِيُّ ٱلۡعَظِيمُ ٢٥٥\nThis noble verse is the greatest, best and most sublime verse in the Quran due to the great matters and noble attributes it contains. For this reason, many Prophetic Hadiths have been narrated encouraging people to recite it and make it a part of their daily recitation, morning and evening, when they go to sleep and after the prescribed prayers. Al-Saadi: 110.\nWhy is it recommended to recite Ayat Al-Kursi regularly at different times of day and night? Why is it the greatest verse in the Quran?\nمَن ذَا ٱلَّذِي يَشۡفَعُ عِندَهُۥٓ إِلَّا بِإِذۡنِهِۦۚ\nThis verse asserts Allah's greatness, majesty and pride, glory be to Him, that no one dares to intercede for anyone with Him except by His permission. Ibn Kathir: 1/292.\nWhat does the requirement of Allah Almighty's permission for those who want to intercede indicate?\nلَآ إِكۡرَاهَ فِي ٱلدِّينِۖ\nThere is no need to compel anyone to believe in it. Compulsion can only be in matters that are ambiguous and unclear, for which there is no proof or evidence, or for matters to which people have a natural aversion. As for this true religion and straight path, it is very clear to those who possess reason, and is based on clear evidence. Truth stands out clear from error, so if one who is fortunate looks at it briefly, he will choose it, whereas the one who has ulterior motives, bad intentions, and evil inclinations will see the truth, yet will prefer falsehood to it; he will see what is beautiful but will choose what is ugly. Allah has no need to compel such a person to follow this religion because there is no benefit in doing so, since the faith of one who is forced to believe is invalid. Al-Saadi: 111.\nWhy is there no need to compel anyone to accept Islam?\nفَمَن يَكۡفُرۡ بِٱلطَّٰغُوتِ وَيُؤۡمِنۢ بِٱللَّهِ فَقَدِ ٱسۡتَمۡسَكَ بِٱلۡعُرۡوَةِ ٱلۡوُثۡقَىٰ لَا ٱنفِصَامَ لَهَاۗ وَٱللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٢٥٦\nSince rejection of falsehood and belief in Allah is something that is uttered by the tongue and believed in the heart, it was best to mention the corresponding attributes of Allah: (All-Hearing) He Who hears what is uttered, (All-Knowing) He Who knows what is believed. Al-Qurtubi: 4/285.\nThe verse concludes with Allah's Attributes: (All-Hearing) and (All-Knowing). Why?\nwords\nخُلَّةٌFriendship\nالقَيُّومُThe All-Sustaining\nسِنَةٌDoziness\nکرسیہFootstool of The Lord\nيَؤُودُهُDoes not tire Him"]])